{"title":"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Additional_Trigonometry-Free_Alternative\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Additional Trigonometry-Free Alternative</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convex\" title=\"Convex\">convex</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon\" title=\"Pentagon\">pentagon</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c2900ad4618e06af726afd8932350149cdc91f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\parallel CE, BC \\parallel AD, AC \\parallel DE, \\angle ABC=120^\\circ, AB=3, BC=5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"514\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7603d09bce85420b6c03d18a7a6c2a9e800aa14a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /> Given that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> between the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53edfea598d4df972d5088afc31d8802b15b674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBD$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271cdd78c4c10cde94410584ce7282874413cb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95eaca439ccbf2863a43b05f4de566ccdabdc392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8c29be3ced461f05a926df28cdf91c3cee631b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\parallel CE, BC \\parallel AD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f1237d9a22aac32265985a19bcc51472a4e62409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCF$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelogram\" title=\"Parallelogram\">parallelogram</a>, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd4cec29c06a26aa67ce81bca3f02b2b73900b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\cong \\triangle CFA$\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />. Also, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f33127da7079f3e0385ffdfe0c2451b6a2c73b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\parallel DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c974577afd255f1d0ea5c89d144a7f3912892c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle EFD$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cd3a7b01b1890253f69e698559c0a908b73dde5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black+linewidth(0.7);  pair D=(0,0), E=(15,0), F=IP(CR(D, 75/7), CR(E, 45/7)), A=D+ (5+(75/7))/(75/7) * (F-D), C = E+ (3+(45/7))/(45/7) * (F-E), B=IP(CR(A,3), CR(C,5));  D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A,(1,0))--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,N)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,NW)--MP(&quot;D&quot;,D)--MP(&quot;E&quot;,E)--cycle); D(D--A--C--E); D(MP(&quot;F&quot;,F)); MP(&quot;5&quot;,(B+C)/2,NW); MP(&quot;3&quot;,(A+B)/2,NE); MP(&quot;15&quot;,(D+E)/2); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"158\" /></center>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c9becb581c151c8520289fc92300bbcee17ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^2 = 3^2 + 5^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 \\cos 120^{\\circ} = 49 \\Longrightarrow AC = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"399\" height=\"16\" />. Thus the length similarity ratio between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1466d39d58bc05988b392a3896a87c06cb8ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b3c9da5f86bf38e06f1eef650cc0cb4438182d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AC}{ED} = \\frac{7}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"39\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/42728e8a0d8ed3b5bdc7e393f3dd929cfb833aec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f669b7c69be6d4e8d8041c405a5f4b5c0bf8d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{BDE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> be the lengths of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitudes</a> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f9b9c18ed140dd23e42e3b5f83d166d250febb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle BDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb20913bc34a4a2aa4b60bbd9a0e70893db1107c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC, DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. Then, the ratio of the areas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe92f35ca6c9d0e7a182ced5636cfa677de50ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[ABC]}{[BDE]} = \\frac{\\frac 12 \\cdot h_{ABC} \\cdot AC}{\\frac 12 \\cdot h_{BDE} \\cdot DE} = \\frac{7}{15} \\cdot \\frac{h_{ABC}}{h_{BDE}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"303\" height=\"47\" />. \n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab74975884ced8df118fd2052f51e522f66fb2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{BDE} = h_{ABC} + h_{CAF} + h_{EFD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"238\" height=\"15\" />, with all three heights oriented in the same direction. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd4cec29c06a26aa67ce81bca3f02b2b73900b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\cong \\triangle CFA$\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3a6cdc41be101658b50b94d527e81ce81b84af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{ABC} = h_{CAF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, and from the similarity ratio, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b6d4ceb45a9fba6a0e54ae406b9b55b2996c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{EFD} = \\frac{15}{7}h_{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc30a8cf6818799d7c66600d7bb5fc3cb2cdd29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h_{ABC}}{h_{BDE}} = \\frac{h_{ABC}}{2h_{ABC} + \\frac {15}7h_{ABC}} = \\frac{7}{29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"257\" height=\"46\" />, and the ratio of the areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/17013c5a3deb428244815aee7972702f6e5c3c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{15} \\cdot \\frac 7{29} = \\frac{49}{435}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/2706b97edc05cfb7b2bd2bd6a7e04cf7c8f015cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{484}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Additional_Trigonometry-Free_Alternative\">Additional Trigonometry-Free Alternative</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Additional Trigonometry-Free Alternative\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Instead of using the Law of Cosines, we can draw a line perpendicular to line BC down from point A until it intersects BC at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c09587109254331a8af5737fbfee3874aff5230b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBA = 60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />, we can use the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangle to deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd17726513947cdaeacdc6117b966d8061d0a9d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d88464279d557548b520eafe217b6c81765f5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"43\" />. From here, we can use Pythagorean theorem to deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b36b86ac878ee1b707085fe4ae5a913e78e631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Then, we can follow with the rest of the solution above.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II\" title=\"2004 AIME II\">2004 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016224657\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 284/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7905/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.289      1 -total\n 58.23%    7.156      1 Template:AIME_box\n 40.00%    4.916      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2692:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016224657 and revision id 191891. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}